{
 "_about": "Named-institution detection for transaction_intelligence/competition. Patterns match the cleaned merchant core (card prefix, date and time stripped, upper-cased) as whole tokens; the longest matching pattern wins. Tiers carry a kind: competitor (counted in penetration and dollars) or adjacency (payment ecosystems, reported apart and counted only on ACH/check). Per-client local banks and credit unions go under LocalCompetitors in clients_config.json -- a list of names, or {name: [aliases]}; they land in the Local Bank / CU tier. No Fed-district tables: the data names the counterparties, the CSM names the locals.",
 "_source": "legacy analytics/competition/01_competitor_config.py (universal + ecosystems only) cut to ~50 institutions, plus the issuers, captives, mortgage servicers and brokerages 1615's first runs surfaced; 2026-08-19",
